    "result": "Excellent! Let me create a final summary and verify everything is complete. Let me run a quick sanity check on the entire implementation by reviewing the key sections:\n\n**Implementation Complete!** \n\nHere's what I've implemented to add threshold validation to `frai eval`:\n\n## Core Changes\n\n### 1. **frai-core** (SDK support)\n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**: Enhanced `generateReport` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n  - Calculates threshold pass/fail for each metric\n  - Adds `passed` boolean and `thresholds` list to report when thresholds provided\n  - Treats null scores as threshold failures\n  \n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**: Updated markdown renderer\n  - Added \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n  - Displays metric name, min requirement, actual score\n\n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`**: Added comprehensive tests\n  - Passing thresholds\n  - Failing thresholds  \n  - Null scores failing thresholds\n  - No thresholds not adding fields\n\n### 2. **frai-cli** (Command-line support)\n- **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**: Added threshold handling\n  - New `parseAndValidateThresholds` function to parse `metric=min` format with full validation\n  - Updated `runEvalCommand` to integrate thresholds and handle exit codes\n  - Added `--threshold` option to eval command with multi-use accumulator\n  \nExit codes:\n- **0**: All thresholds pass or no thresholds provided\n- **1**: Any threshold fails\n- **2**: Invalid threshold (bad format, out-of-range min, unknown metric)\n\n### 3. **Documentation**\n- Updated `README.md` with threshold option documentation\n- Updated `docs/eval_harness_design.md` with threshold validation in MVP scope\n\n## Feature Highlights\n\n\u2705 Metric with no score (null) fails threshold instead of crashing  \n\u2705 Reports written either way (success or failure)  \n\u2705 Threshold values validated to be between 0 and 1  \n\u2705 Unknown metrics flagged with helpful error listing valid metric IDs  \n\u2705 Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`  \n\u2705 SDK users can call `generateReport({ thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 } })`  \n\u2705 Without `--threshold`, behavior unchanged  \n\nThe implementation is production-ready and satisfies all requirements in the feature request.",
